<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5276" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμιλλ-άομαι</span></b> : fut.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					950
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				349c
			</span></i>: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμιλλήθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.), <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.31
			</span></i>; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμιλλησάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Arat.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Par.</u>
				51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				1.127
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				149
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, etc.: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίλλημαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr. <i><span class="en">
				11.1
			</span></i>):—<i>compete, vie, contend,</i> Ar.l.c., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἀλλήλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.: c. dat.pers., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				127
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HF</u>
					960
				</span></i>
			: c. dat. rei, <i>contend in</i> or <i>with</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμιλληθεὶς λόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					195
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>HF</u>
				1255
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					426
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵπποις, τόξοις,</span> etc.,
				<i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				328a
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				834a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>
			<i>about</i> or <i>for</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Charid.</u>
				20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					10.31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				830e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				968b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρ τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.86.8
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ. ὡς</span> . . or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπως</span> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				349c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				7.2.14
			</span></i>: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ. στάδιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					833a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in pass. sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλλ᾽ ἁμιλληθέντα</span>”
				<i>made subjects of contest,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					812.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> without idea
			of rivalry, <i>strive, hasten eagerly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὸ ἄκρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					3.4.44
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span> to obtain a thing,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				490a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1162b8
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῦρ᾽ ἁμιλλᾶται ποδί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					456
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὲ τὴν ὄρεγμα δεινὸν ἡμιλλημένην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					546
				</span></i>
			: metaph., c. acc. cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποῖον
				ἁμιλλᾱθῶ γόον;</span> how shall I groan loud enough?
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				165
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόνδ᾽ ἁμιλλῶμαι λόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hec.</u>
					271
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has 
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμιλλᾶν: ἐρίζειν, καὶ εἰς
				τάχος γράφειν.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
